# Proposed features recognized from split_hole.step by sidecar/import_step.py
# (contract v1 -- see sidecar/CONTRACT.md). Review before use:
# recognition proposes, it does not machine.

# F3: planar, normal +Z, topmost planar face (CHECKLIST row 1.1)
feature F3_Top Plane(z=20.0)

# F10: outer profile under top cap F3: vertical wall loop F1 F2 F10 F4, top at z=20.0, base at z=12.0, material inside the loop; stepped base: the profile stops at the highest base z=12.0, and F1 to z=0.0, F2 to z=0.0, F4 to z=0.0 run on below it; the base at z=12.0 is the head's own underside (the face under the walls faces down): the wall is traced from above, the underside is the other setup's (CHECKLIST row 2.2)
# consume with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F10_Profile, comp=control)  [the feature carries its own z + extent]
# the loop is wound CW: material inside, tool outside (the winding convention,
# DECISIONS.md -> "Row-2.4 side selector")
# comp=control is required on Contour runs: recognized boundaries carry rounded
# corners tessellated to chords, and engine comp hard-errors on rounded-corner
# offsets (DECISIONS.md -> "recognized contours propose comp=control")
# the base is stepped: this profile stops at z=12.0, the highest base; the walls F1 F2 F4 run on below it
# and belong to whatever stands lower -- declare that by hand or accept its own proposal
# the base at z=12.0 is an overhang: the face under the walls faces down, so the
# tool has air under it at the base; the underside itself is the other setup's
feature F10_Profile ProfileBoss(z=20.0, extent=8.0
    0.0 0.0
    0.0 30.0
    40.0 30.0
    40.0 0.0
)

# F11: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material outside (a bore), opens upward; bottom opens through -- a drillable through hole (CHECKLIST row 2.3)
# consume with: run Form(points=[F11_Hole], tool=..., cycle=Simple)  [the bore carries its own extent, measured down from the stock top]
# through hole -- drill past extent=20.0 by the tip's point length for full-diameter breakthrough
# or finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F11_Hole, stepover=...)
feature F11_Hole CylinderBore(dia=4.0, extent=20.0, x=10.0, y=15.0)

# F13: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material outside (a bore), opens upward; bottom opens through -- a drillable through hole; rim at z=8.0, 12.0 below the stock top z=20.0, with open air straight above it to the top -- proposed from the top, where a drill through the blank starts, extent 20.0 the whole way down; what the model has above the rim is another feature's to cut; wall F12 is the same hole, 4.0 of air between them, z=8.0 to z=12.0 -- one hole, drilled once from the top (CHECKLIST row 2.3)
# consume with: run Form(points=[F13_Hole], tool=..., cycle=Simple)  [the bore carries its own extent, measured down from the stock top]
# through hole -- drill past extent=20.0 by the tip's point length for full-diameter breakthrough
# or finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F13_Hole, stepover=...)
# the model interrupts this hole (walls F13 and F12, 4.0 of air between them, z=8.0 to z=12.0): drilled
# through the uncut blank it is one plain hole; drilled after the gap is cut, the
# drill breaks out and starts again on the far side
feature F13_Hole CylinderBore(dia=4.0, extent=20.0, x=32.0, y=15.0)
